<article class="env-lemma" id="0F1W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F1W">Lemma <span data-tag="0F1W">37.66.4</span>.</a> Any quasi-affine morphism is ind-quasi-affine. Any immersion is ind-quasi-affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first assertion is immediate from the definitions. In particular, affine morphisms, such as closed immersions, are ind-quasi-affine. Thus, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F1V" data-tag="0F1V">37.66.3</a>, it remains to show that an open immersion is ind-quasi-affine. This, however, is immediate from the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>